          {
            "title": "Using numbers",
            "id": 126240,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>I nomi delle variabili possono contenere anche dei <strong>numeri</strong>. Aggiungere numeri è utile quando ci sono più variabili simili. Creiamo qui la variabile <code>car1</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"swift\" name=\"main.swift\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" car1\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"1 car\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>car1</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Giving a variable a value",
            "id": 126241,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Dopo aver creato e denominato una variabile, usiamo il segno <code>=</code> per memorizzarvi un <strong>valore</strong>. Ad esempio, <code>let city = \"Chicago\"</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"swift\" name=\"main.swift\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" city = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Chicago&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"9\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>=</code>, seguito da <code>\"Chicago\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "String",
            "id": 126243,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>I valori che abbiamo memorizzato, come <code>\"Chicago\"</code>, sono <strong>stringhe</strong>. Le stringhe sono parole racchiuse tra virgolette doppie.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"swift\" name=\"main.swift\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Chicago&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"9\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"</code>, seguito da <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Sentence",
            "id": 126244,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Le string possono contenere ogni tipo di lettera e simbolo, inclusi gli spazi. Ad esempio, <code>\"Winter is coming.\"</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"swift\" name=\"main.swift\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Winter is coming.&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"1\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"</code>, seguito da <code>Winter is coming.</code> e infine <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
